    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d921">

                <pb facs="0744" n="668" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg668"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/7698a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Mr.
                            Parker, representing American
                        interests</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d921-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 15, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Scott-Obregon conference amicably concluded, but without definite result.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d921-f2"/> Both Governments continuing negotiations. Surface
                    indications do not presage any untoward incident. You should be extremely alert,
                    however, to guard yourself and Americans, your district, against sudden hostile
                    developments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d921-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d921-f1-content">
                <p>Same to American Consuls at Guadalajara, Monterey, Tampico, Vera Cruz, Acapulco,
                    Hermosillo, Mazatlan, Manzanillo, Salina Cruz, Frontera and Progreso.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d921-f2" n="2" xml:id="d921-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">See</hi> Political Affairs, ante, <ref target="#pg527"
                        >p. 527</ref>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">et seq.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
